[Music]  hey everyone its Johanna here today  we'll be making some easy delicious  gluten-free vegetarian dinners firstly  let's understand what is a gluten-free  diet a gluten-free diet is a diet which  excludes the protein gluten this protein  is found in grains such as wheat barley  rye and cryptically across between wheat  and rye a gluten-free diet is used  primarily to treat people with celiac  disease because gluten causes  inflammation in the small intestines of  people with celiac disease  hence consuming gluten free meals will  help to control the signs and symptoms  of celiac disease and to prevent any  further complications gluten free meals  can also help with people who are gluten  intolerance nowadays gluten free diet is  popular even amongst people who do not  need to go on this diet they are turning  to a gluten-free diet in response to  feeling tired bloated depressed and they  find that by eliminating gluten helps to  make them feel better and to even lose  weight  chances are it's because they are  cutting out excess hidden calories found  in flour-based food and not due to  cutting out gluten if you aim to eat a  balanced meal you will also feel less  bloated and it will also help you  towards your weight loss another  important point to note is that  gluten-free foods do not necessarily  mean healthy or low in calories in fact  gluten-free diet can be nutrient  deficient low in fiber iron vitamin B  and D and many more other essential  nutrients that's because majority of the  gluten-free products are made from  refined and Irish  grains and starches which can be high in  calories with very few minerals and  vitamins so if you plan to go on a  gluten-free diet it is very important  for you to make the extra effort to  consume more vegetables fruits beans  lean meat and more natural gluten free  grains such as rice quinoa and buckwheat  instead of just buying products with  gluten-free label audits my gluten-free  dinners are cooked using mainly  unprocessed natural ingredients so let's  start with my really easy and cheap  recipe which is also part of my lazy  dinner - mutter rice and black beans  this dinner takes less than 15 minutes  to prepare so when I'm feeling tired or  lazy and I want something nutritious and  feeling I will opt for this the  ingredients you need are 1/2 a cup of  uncooked brown or white rice which will  weigh approximately 240 gram once cooked  half a can of chopped tomatoes juice  reserved 1 TSP of olive oil 2 cloves of  garlic minced 1 large bell pepper  chopped half the can of black beans  rinsed and drained 1 teaspoon of ground  cumin 1/2 a teaspoon of chili powder and  a little bit of salt for seasoning the  first step is to cook the rice according  to instructions in a pan heat olive oil  over medium-high heat add garlic and  bell pepper and fry for three to four  minutes until fragrant and bell pepper  starts to soften then mix in the black  beans chili powder cumin and salt and  cook for another 1 minute to combine all  the ingredients together next and half a  can of chopped tomatoes and bring to a  boil under low heat cook for another 5  to 7  until the beans have absorbed much of  the liquid finally mix in the rice and  combine all the ingredients stirring for  one to two minutes until the rice is  warm and it's served immediately why do  I like rice with black beans well  firstly one cup of black beans has 15  grams of satisfying protein and it does  not contain any saturated fat found in  animal protein sources especially red  meat black beans are also a low energy  dense food which means you get to eat  more for less calories this can help you  to avoid overeating and to watch your  calorie intake which can help to with  weight loss ultimate in a healthy weight  and by combining rice and beans to  incomplete proteins on their own they  become a complete protein this one  serving only has 292 calories so try my  lazy and cheap dinner the next recipe is  one of my favorite dishes which is  usually high in calories and fat lasagna  so after gaining inspirations from  several recipes and trying my own  combination with ingredients that I like  I present to you my low calorie  vegetarian quinoa lasagna it looks so  unhealthy but it is so healthy packed  full of vegetables to make this lasagna  the ingredients you need are 1 cup of  water half a cup of quinoa uncooked 2  teaspoons of olive oil 1 medium onion  diced one curve of garlic minced one jar  of basic traditional pasta sauce or  tomato sauce half a block of firm tofu 1  large egg beaten juice from half a lemon  1 large zucchini sliced 1 large bell  pepper slice 1 large carrot diced salt  and pepper for seasoning and half a cup  of grated cheese of your choice  Parmesan cheddar mozzarella pour a  dairy-free cheese in a pan combine water  and quinoa and bring to a boil then  reduce to a simmer cover and cook for 15  minutes while waiting for the quinoa to  cook in a food processor combine the  tofu with an egg and lemon juice blend  for 20 seconds or until you have a  smooth and creamy mixture and set it  aside  once quinoa is cooked block with a fork  and spread the quinoa evenly in an  ovenproof dish now preheat the oven to  180 degrees Celsius or 350 degrees  Fahrenheit in a pan keeps 1 TSP of olive  oil over medium-high heat add onion and  garlic and cooked for three to four  minutes until fragrant and lightly Brown  add the carrots and cook for another  three to four minutes then add the pasta  sauce or tomato sauce stir for three to  four minutes until the sauce is hot  remove from heat and set it aside next  he is the remaining 1 teaspoon of olive  oil over medium-high heat at bell pepper  and zucchini season with salt and pepper  and cook for 10 minutes or until the  vegetables are tender and set it aside  finally let's start to layer our lasagna  spread half of the pasta sauce over the  quinoa make a layer of half of the  vegetables then pour the creamy tofu  mixture then the remaining vegetables  finished with the remaining pasta sauce  and spread cheese evenly on top now it's  time to place it in the oven bake the  lasagne for 30 to 35 minutes and - it's  hot and the cheese is melted bubbling  and slightly brown around the edges then  remove from the oven and allow the  lasagne to cool down  ten minutes before serving here are my  reasons why you should try this instead  of using lasagna noodles which mostly is  included free I've substituted with one  of the world's healthiest food quinoa  most grains are considered incomplete  protein sources because they do not  contain all the essential amino acids  quinoa however is considered a complete  protein source containing all nine  essential amino acids  besides that quinoa contains almost  twice as much fiber in comparison to  most other grains and with all the  vegetables in this lasagna it is packed  full of fiber so this dish will keep you  satisfied for longer and instead of  using the typical white lasagna sauce  which is high in calories and high in  fat I have made my own white sauce using  tofu and egg which is low in calories  high in protein and low in fat if you  are a vegan you can omit the egg which  shouldn't really affect the recipe and  taste by much and you can use dairy-free  cheese zucchini and carrots are low in  calories and high in water content so by  consuming these vegetables you will be  adding to your daily fluid needs most  traditional pasta sauces are gluten-free  but please do read the food label and  check the ingredients just to be sure or  you can make your own sauce with tomato  puree and tomato sauce and a little bit  of mixed herbs so if you are craving for  lasagna but you're concerned about the  high calorie and fat content try my  healthy quinoa lasagna instead this one  serving only has 200 and I think three  point six calories so you can feel good  when eating it  my final dinner on the menu is an Asian  dish chickpeas spinach curry  this is a basic vegetable curry recipe  so feel free to change the vegetables  according to your own preference the  ingredients you'll need are 1/2 an onion  diced 1 clove of garlic crushed 1  teaspoon of curry powder 1 TSP of olive  oil 1 can of chickpeas rinsed and  drained half the can of chopped tomatoes  I'm drained 150 grams of fresh or frozen  spinach 150 gram of fresh or frozen  cauliflower 1/2 a cup of water and salt  and pepper to taste in a pan heat olive  oil over medium-high heat add onion and  garlic and lightly stir fry for 3 to 4  minutes until slightly brown and  fragrant then mix in the curry powder  and a splash of water and cook for  another minute next add the chickpeas  cauliflower tomatoes and season with  salt and pepper cover and allow all the  ingredients to cook for 15 to 20 minutes  stirring occasionally  finally stir in the spinach every mini  water cook for another 5 to 7 minutes or  until spinach is fully wilted and warm  and serve if you like hard spice I have  made this with you in mind this one  serving only has 169 calories you can  serve this with a side of rice or even  baked potato this recipe is also part of  my 90 day weight loss challenge vegan  meal plans so have this as part of a  balanced diet now remember that all my  recipes are always interchangeable so  you can have this for your life as well  well you might ask me should I go under  gluten-free  personally I am not limited to free diet  because there is no need to and I do  enjoy my occasional naughty food your  dietary choice is up to you if you think  that you might have celiac disease or  gluten intolerance do not self diagnose  go to your local doctor to get an  accurate diagnosis of your symptoms if  you want to go on a gluten-free diet do  take the time to consider the extra food  shopping cost and the lifestyle changes  and sacrifices you might have to make  gluten-free or not do try this easy and  delicious dinner recipes and let me know  which is your favorite in the comments  below for new Fitness food and  motivational videos please like share  and subscribe to my You Tube channel and  website do you follow me on Facebook  Instagram and Twitter  to stay connected with me thanks guys  [Music]

